		"setup.run_tips_on": "Marina's tips: on",
		"setup.run_tips_off": "Marina's tips: off",
		"setup.run_tips_hint": "Marina from HR explains how things work in the chat during your first month.",
		"tip.assign": "Hello, I'm Marina from HR, and I'll be helping you out this first week. Tasks land in the Inbox: click a card, then a person, and it's theirs. Who's good at what, you'll see from the results.",
		"tip.pushback": "Pushing back is normal. There are different ways to talk people round, and each one responds to something different. Just don't say Irina asked if she didn't: she checks.",
		"tip.end_day": "Once you've handed out what you think is right, hit End the day. The work happens in the evening, and you'll see how it went in the chat.",
		"tip.evening": "That's how a day goes. People here don't get tired from work, they get tired from overtime and from work that's beyond them. There's always more work than hands, you can't do it all, and that's fine.",
		"tip.talk": "Talk to people one on one, that's how you learn what makes them tick. Just remember the dots at the top are your attention for the day, and it runs out.",
		"tip.decline": "You don't have to take everything. A card in the Inbox has Turn down, only whoever brought it may go and complain to Irina.",
		"tip.intervene": "If someone has been sitting on a task for a while, open it in the In progress column and hit Step in. Sometimes they're just looking in the wrong place.",
		"tip.overtime": "See \"staying late today\" on someone? That's overtime. Now and then is fine, but that's what wears people out. They'll recover over the weekend.",
		"tip.friday": "Friday is the week's report: who worked how much. Then Irina goes over the week and asks who gets the credit and who takes the blame. Think about what you'll say.",
		"tip.run.assign": "Hello, I'm Marina from HR, and I'll be helping you out this first month. Tasks land in the Inbox: click a card, then a person. Each hand-out costs a point, those are the dots at the top, so you won't get to hand out everything, and you don't need to.",
		"tip.run.start_work": "Once you've handed out what you think is right, hit Get to work. That's the morning done, and the cards you didn't hand out will wait in the Inbox.",
		"tip.run.midday": "Midday, when you can see who's struggling with what. You can sit with someone over a task, step in, or just have a talk. When you've done enough, hit End the day.",
		"tip.run.evening": "If you ran out of points, you borrowed from tomorrow, and you'll have fewer then. The weekend clears the debt, but three days in a row in debt and you'll go down.",
		"tip.run.standup": "See, someone took a card on their own? You can thank them or take it back. Or say nothing, which is free, but people will take it as a yes.",
		"tip.run.pushback": "Pushing back is normal. There are different ways to talk people round, and each one responds to something different.",
		"tip.run.penalty": "Every card says what missing it will cost. Sometimes Irina just remembers, sometimes there's a fine or more fires in the deck.",
		"tip.run.decline": "You don't have to take everything. A card has Turn down, only whoever brought it may take offence.",
		"tip.run.upgrades": "Money isn't only for salaries. Have a look at the upgrade tree: a rollout costs money and effort, but then some of the routine goes away for good.",
		"tip.run.friday": "Friday is payday, so keep an eye on the money. And at the end of the month Irina splits the budget between you and Taras by who got how much done.",
